WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.960
<v Mishu>Back to the tailor's shop. Listen carefully.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.640
<v Mother>Make it four longer.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.775
<v Ishita>Four fingers, of course!

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.101
<v Rohan>No way. Four metres!

00:00:11.101 --> 00:00:15.849
<v Mishu>Four what? Four fingers? Four centimetres? Four metres?

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:18.811
<v Mishu>That would be a very long uniform!

00:00:18.811 --> 00:00:20.788
<v Rohan>It would go right out of the door!

00:00:20.788 --> 00:00:26.225
<v Mishu>So a measurement needs two things: a number, how many, and a unit, of what.

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:30.089
<v Mishu>Four is the number. Angula, or centimetre, is the unit.

00:00:30.089 --> 00:00:33.900
<v Ishita>A number and a unit. Never one without the other!
